WEBVTT

00:00:56.431 --> 00:01:01.687
Was any of this for good or bad?
I really couldn't say.

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:07.359
But like most people, I guess...

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:11.071
I was born and raised
in the same country.

00:01:12.281 --> 00:01:17.119
My family was middle-class,
pretty ordinary.

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:21.915
And so, I've never known
the troubles of the rich...

00:01:21.999 --> 00:01:24.167
or the hardships of the poor.

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:27.212
To tell you the truth,
I could really care less.

00:01:29.965 --> 00:01:33.176
When I was a kid,
I wanted to be a Navy pilot.

00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:37.681
You had to join the Navy
if you wanted to fly jets.

00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:42.936
They were so fast and
flew so high...

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.940
For me, there could be
nothing better than flying.

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:51.653
But 2 months before
I was to graduate from school...

00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:57.367
I saw that my grades weren't good
enough to let me do any of that.

00:01:58.702 --> 00:02:02.414
And so... I ended up
joining the Space Force.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:09.671
<i>"Royal Space F0rce- The Wings of Honnéamise"</i>

00:05:02.177 --> 00:05:04.513
I just want to
know two things.

00:05:04.638 --> 00:05:08.850
Where have you been?! And why
aren't you in dress uniform?!

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:13.230
Might I assume the first question
to be in reference to my past?

00:05:13.355 --> 00:05:17.025
Stop that, damn you!
I'm asking you why you're late!

00:05:17.359 --> 00:05:20.862
Why do you always
have to play the clown?

00:05:20.946 --> 00:05:24.616
You don't think this is serious?
Coming late to a comrade's funeral!

00:05:24.699 --> 00:05:27.494
I was taking a nap
and overslept, sir!

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:32.207
A man in your own
unit is dead, and you...

00:05:32.958 --> 00:05:35.335
you call yourself
a soldier?!

00:05:38.713 --> 00:05:41.174
Forget it.
Just get in line.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:48.515
- Hey there.

00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:49.599
- Hey there.
- Hi.

00:05:49.808 --> 00:05:52.060
Why are you late?

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:54.563
I was just thinking
about some stuff.

00:05:54.646 --> 00:05:56.731
Why aren't you
in dress uniform'?

00:05:56.857 --> 00:05:59.860
Knock it off. I don't wanna
wear those hideous clothes.

00:06:01.278 --> 00:06:03.905
Heh, he thinks he's the general now.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:07.284
"Coming late to a comrade's
funeral!" He killed the guy!

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.452
It was a test accident, right?

00:06:09.578 --> 00:06:11.913
Yeah, I hear the
police are coming today.

00:06:11.997 --> 00:06:14.291
They think the urine bag ruptured
during the space suit test...

00:06:14.291 --> 00:06:15.834
and shorted
the whole thing out.

00:06:16.668 --> 00:06:19.254
Space suit?
What's that?

00:06:19.337 --> 00:06:22.090
You don't know? It's something
you have to wear in space.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:24.134
He actually wants to
launch somebody up there.

00:06:25.635 --> 00:06:28.096
Manned artificial satellites.

00:06:28.597 --> 00:06:29.764
That's insane.

00:06:29.848 --> 00:06:32.309
Yeah, that crazy bastard.

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:35.854
He's not giving up, though.
The next step's gotta be...

00:06:43.445 --> 00:06:45.947
Space Force anthem, prepare!

00:06:52.829 --> 00:06:55.874
Space Force!
Anthem! In unison!

00:06:56.708 --> 00:07:01.963
"With the solar wind on our backs"

00:07:02.672 --> 00:07:08.053
"In the darkness of the galaxy,
we spread our wings to fly"

00:07:08.637 --> 00:07:13.266
"lnto the chaos covering our path"

00:07:13.975 --> 00:07:18.688
"The time of judgement for
us all is drawing ever near"

00:07:47.342 --> 00:07:50.971
Majaho got some bread
in the mail. Big box of it.

00:07:51.054 --> 00:07:52.889
Why bread?

00:07:53.848 --> 00:07:56.893
'Cause his family
owns a bakery.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.480
Bread, huh?

00:08:00.563 --> 00:08:04.734
Yeah. A bakery'd be nice.
You think they'd hire me'?

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:09.739
Count me out. Probably couldn't
get another job on the outside.

00:08:10.657 --> 00:08:12.575
This place is great.

00:08:13.034 --> 00:08:16.371
At least we don't have to worry
about running out of food here.

00:08:17.038 --> 00:08:20.667
We get hungry because we are alive.
The same for why we can eat...

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.546
I don't wanna die here...

00:08:24.671 --> 00:08:25.630
Ow!

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:30.802
Lots of free time, Shiro?

00:08:31.553 --> 00:08:35.473
I didn't realize your job
here was to take naps!

00:08:36.766 --> 00:08:40.437
You know what this is?
A one <i>deem</i> coin.

00:08:40.562 --> 00:08:43.857
It can buy you a loaf of
bread or a bottle of oil.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:47.944
But they say a Khozel bandit
would kill a man for one of these.

00:08:48.695 --> 00:08:50.613
So, if you think about it,
it's worth quite a lot.

00:08:50.739 --> 00:08:54.659
Overtime pay. Getting an advance
should make you weep with joy!

00:08:54.743 --> 00:08:57.412
And now from you
I want 300 push-ups.

00:08:57.537 --> 00:08:59.497
If you're doing sit-ups,
it'll be 500!

00:09:19.809 --> 00:09:22.520
<i>Tekatta/ Tekatta/
Get it</i> while <i>it's hot!</i>

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.621
Why'd you come in uniform'?

00:09:40.288 --> 00:09:43.917
Had to. With all that extra work,
I didn't have time to change.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.920
Embarrassing.
Keep away from me.

00:09:47.087 --> 00:09:50.548
Any gal who sees you
in that thing will just laugh at you.

00:09:51.216 --> 00:09:54.469
Any lady who's heard of
the Space Force would laugh.

00:09:54.552 --> 00:09:56.679
If there was an Army soldier who's
never walked on the ground...

00:09:56.805 --> 00:09:58.556
hell, I would laugh, too.

00:10:05.772 --> 00:10:08.817
To the spaceship, and the men who passed away.

00:10:19.994 --> 00:10:22.455
You think the old
man's really serious?

00:10:22.539 --> 00:10:24.541
People wouldn't be getting
killed if it was just a game.

00:10:24.707 --> 00:10:27.460
But most people think
of manned space flight...

00:10:27.544 --> 00:10:29.379
as something
of the far future.

00:10:29.504 --> 00:10:32.549
I don't think our Force will
last that far into the future.

00:10:33.216 --> 00:10:36.427
I just hope it'll hold out
till I can find a new job.

00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:38.138
Ask Majaho for one.

00:10:38.221 --> 00:10:41.224
Hit! Hit! Four, three.

00:10:41.724 --> 00:10:45.145
Son of a...!
Two more down.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:51.192
That's a strange uniform.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:57.866
It's for the Space Force.

00:10:57.991 --> 00:11:01.703
Space Force? What, are we
gonna get attacked by aliens?

00:11:03.246 --> 00:11:04.455
Well, "Lt. Colonel"?

00:11:04.539 --> 00:11:07.125
Knock it off! You're a
"major," for God's sake!

00:11:07.834 --> 00:11:10.837
Two, three, two, one, two!

00:11:11.337 --> 00:11:14.424
For crying out loud, Matti!
Pick on someone else for a change!

00:11:14.549 --> 00:11:16.676
Oh, I give up.

00:11:17.051 --> 00:11:21.472
Don't be so down. The night's
just getting started, eh?

00:11:30.023 --> 00:11:34.903
Hey, gorgeous!
Look over here!

00:11:36.112 --> 00:11:39.574
Hey, baby!
Don't you hear me'? Hey!

00:11:53.963 --> 00:11:55.590
Come on!

00:11:56.382 --> 00:11:57.675
This way.

00:11:59.677 --> 00:12:02.597
And don't worry about
the money. My treat.

00:12:02.722 --> 00:12:04.724
I just want to go to sleep.

00:12:04.807 --> 00:12:06.059
You came!

00:12:06.142 --> 00:12:07.852
Tohn! Tohn! You're here!

00:12:07.936 --> 00:12:09.479
<i>No, Mat“, you mean.
Mam'.!</i>

00:12:09.604 --> 00:12:12.315
Matti, Matti, Matti, Matti!
I'm glad you came!

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:15.109
I like your perfume today.
Ummm, delicious.

00:12:15.235 --> 00:12:17.862
C'mon, I called a
friend to help out today.

00:12:17.946 --> 00:12:19.489
C'mon, c'mon!

00:12:19.614 --> 00:12:21.908
Uh, hey!
You said you'd treat...

00:12:22.659 --> 00:12:23.534
- A friend, huh?

00:12:23.534 --> 00:12:25.495
- A friend, huh?
- Mimi! Tohn's here!

00:12:29.707 --> 00:12:32.043
Heh, "Tohn," huh?

00:12:54.649 --> 00:12:57.151
The day of
judgement approaches!

00:12:58.361 --> 00:13:01.489
Those who live in sin will
surely be cast into hell!

00:13:02.991 --> 00:13:05.660
Those who ignores the
path of righteousness...

00:13:05.743 --> 00:13:08.288
those who takes no responsibility
for his sins...

00:13:08.371 --> 00:13:10.790
and those who feels no shame
for his transgressions...

00:13:10.873 --> 00:13:12.709
these are all sins!

00:13:15.295 --> 00:13:16.629
Thank you.

00:13:16.713 --> 00:13:18.589
God is weeping for us.

00:13:18.673 --> 00:13:22.635
The day of final judgement which
was promised after mankind first...

00:13:22.719 --> 00:13:26.848
stole the flame from heaven's
ovens is drawing ever near!

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:30.768
We must all be prepared
for when that day arrives...

00:14:03.009 --> 00:14:05.053
Oh, it's you.
Where're the others'?

00:14:05.136 --> 00:14:07.930
It's a holiday today.
You think they'd come back?

00:14:08.222 --> 00:14:12.101
"Please come"? What,
a new whorehouse opened up?

00:14:12.226 --> 00:14:14.145
Oh, and there's
an address, too!

00:14:14.228 --> 00:14:16.189
Ah, knock it off.

00:14:22.195 --> 00:14:23.529
Can I use your foam?

00:14:23.613 --> 00:14:26.616
He who has to beg for foam
is doomed to be a beggar.

00:14:27.617 --> 00:14:30.286
Oh, and you really shouldn't
sleep in a dead man's bed.

00:14:30.411 --> 00:14:32.038
Not good for health.

00:14:32.705 --> 00:14:33.498
Ouch!

00:15:16.165 --> 00:15:18.334
Hello, little guy.
You live here'?

00:15:42.817 --> 00:15:45.987
Excuse me'? I came because
I saw your flyer.

00:15:52.326 --> 00:15:55.079
Come in!
Come in! Come in! Come in!

00:15:56.664 --> 00:16:00.501
Come right on in!
You're just in time.

00:16:00.626 --> 00:16:02.962
I was about
to make some tea.

00:16:03.045 --> 00:16:06.299
Here, please!
Have a seat!

00:16:06.466 --> 00:16:08.593
I've got some ferr/sh
cooking in the oven.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:11.971
You were able to find
the place all right?

00:16:12.513 --> 00:16:14.932
Uh, yeah.
I took the trolley out here.

00:16:15.016 --> 00:16:18.269
My name's
Riqunni Nonderaiko.

00:16:18.352 --> 00:16:20.480
Shirotsugh Lhadatt.

00:16:20.563 --> 00:16:22.815
Pleased to meet you,
Mr. Lhadatt.

00:16:22.899 --> 00:16:24.192
Please, just
call me Shirotsugh.

00:16:24.317 --> 00:16:27.153
Okay, Shirotsugh.
This is wonderful.

00:16:27.236 --> 00:16:29.947
Someone actually came!
How do you take your <i>muuk?</i>

00:16:30.198 --> 00:16:32.408
Strong, please.
Nothing in it.

00:16:34.785 --> 00:16:36.579
So, how old are you, boy'?

00:16:36.704 --> 00:16:40.041
Oh, Mama's a little girl.

00:16:40.124 --> 00:16:43.294
Manna, bring the
nice man a plate.

00:16:51.552 --> 00:16:53.095
Thanks...

00:16:53.596 --> 00:16:57.225
I've never seen Manna take to
a stranger so quickly before.

00:16:57.308 --> 00:16:58.684
Here we are.

00:17:00.269 --> 00:17:02.897
Kids just like me,
I guess.

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:06.901
There you go.
Sorry if it's overdone.

00:17:07.735 --> 00:17:11.405
No, no. Terr/sh tastes better
when it's a little overcooked.

00:17:11.531 --> 00:17:14.408
Really, it looks delicious.
Let's eat!

00:17:21.165 --> 00:17:23.709
The tea smells
really good, too...

00:17:28.256 --> 00:17:30.174
That was good tea.

00:17:30.883 --> 00:17:33.970
But you're right, times
really are terrible nowadays.

00:17:34.095 --> 00:17:37.348
Adults can no longer judge
what's right and wrong.

00:17:37.431 --> 00:17:40.393
Exactly! And they aren't
bringing kids up right, either.

00:17:40.476 --> 00:17:42.562
The whole world's
just screwed up.

00:17:42.645 --> 00:17:47.108
God's hand foretold all
of this... Oh, by the way!

00:17:47.608 --> 00:17:48.568
Yes?

00:17:48.651 --> 00:17:50.361
You haven't said
what's bothering you.

00:17:50.736 --> 00:17:55.992
Yeah, well... There was
an accident where I work.

00:17:56.117 --> 00:17:57.243
I see.

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:00.788
And a good friend of
mine died because of it.

00:18:00.913 --> 00:18:03.958
That's terrible.
You must be really upset.

00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:08.796
Yeah, and now I can't seem to
eat or do my job or any...

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.343
So, what sort of
job do you have?

00:18:15.136 --> 00:18:18.723
Uh, well... Have you ever
heard of the Space Force?

00:18:19.307 --> 00:18:20.558
I'm sorry, but...

00:18:20.641 --> 00:18:23.936
You've never heard of it.
I'm not surprised.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.146
- You're a soldier, then?

00:18:25.146 --> 00:18:28.024
- You're a soldier, then?
- Well, we don't fight or anything.

00:18:28.149 --> 00:18:30.610
We're just training
to go into space.

00:18:30.985 --> 00:18:34.405
Oh, space?
You mean to the stars?

00:18:35.615 --> 00:18:37.366
Well, not quite that far.

00:18:37.491 --> 00:18:39.327
What a wonderful
job you have!

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:41.412
Huh? You think so?

00:18:41.621 --> 00:18:43.706
Yes, I think it's great!

00:18:43.831 --> 00:18:46.167
To be free of the
troubles of this world and...

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:49.754
to go to the unspoiled
world of the stars...

00:18:49.837 --> 00:18:52.173
Don't you think
that's wonderful'?

00:18:53.841 --> 00:18:56.802
Yeah... And we're the only
Space Force in the world, too.

00:18:57.762 --> 00:19:00.431
I've never had such
a wonderful holiday.

00:19:00.514 --> 00:19:03.142
To think such a marvelous
person would come and visit me.

00:19:03.351 --> 00:19:06.270
Do you think you can tell
me about the stars sometime?

00:19:06.354 --> 00:19:07.688
Sure. It'd be a pleasure.

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:13.069
Our children will one day
live among the stars, in peace.

00:19:13.444 --> 00:19:18.074
Yeah, and space is so vast.
There are no borders, either!

00:19:18.199 --> 00:19:21.994
It's fantastic!
Soldiers who don't make war!

00:19:22.078 --> 00:19:24.830
Well, we've got
a different purpose...

00:19:24.914 --> 00:19:26.749
than the guys fighting over a lake.

00:19:26.874 --> 00:19:28.376
A higher purpose.

00:19:28.459 --> 00:19:31.962
We're the ones who have to clear
the way to peace for all mankind.

00:19:32.046 --> 00:19:34.382
This world's too
small for the humanity.

00:19:34.465 --> 00:19:38.177
From here on,
it'll be the age of space!

00:19:47.687 --> 00:19:50.898
<i>The chief causes of launch failure
may be divided into two categories.</i>

00:19:50.981 --> 00:19:54.944
<i>Human error
and mechanical failure.</i>

00:19:56.070 --> 00:19:58.739
Morning!
Oh, the morning film lecture, huh?

00:19:58.823 --> 00:20:02.326
These are the only funny movies
we ever get to see around here.

00:20:04.203 --> 00:20:06.330
Hey, you borrowed my bike
yesterday, didn't you?

00:20:06.414 --> 00:20:09.959
Yep, sure did.
Night air felt really good.

00:20:10.084 --> 00:20:12.420
Would it have killed you
to put some gas back in?

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:15.256
Honestly, you worry
about such little things.

00:20:15.381 --> 00:20:17.925
We are the proud
officers of the Space Force.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:20.636
Trifles he worries about!

00:20:20.761 --> 00:20:24.014
We're doing big,
important stuff here!

00:20:24.598 --> 00:20:28.102
Maybe he's got a crack in his head.

00:20:28.644 --> 00:20:29.937
I don't know.

00:20:33.274 --> 00:20:36.694
Gentlemen, you are the proud
members of the Space Force!

00:20:36.777 --> 00:20:40.573
It was 30 years ago that
Khi Lei Kerass published...

00:20:40.656 --> 00:20:42.658
<i>The Possibility
of Galactic Travel.</i>

00:20:42.783 --> 00:20:47.121
It has been about 20 years since
the creation of our Space Force!

00:20:47.621 --> 00:20:52.126
Words cannot describe what has
happened during those 20 years.

00:20:52.626 --> 00:20:55.629
It was really just a drain
dish off of some flowerpot.

00:20:55.755 --> 00:20:57.298
Our first "satellite"!

00:20:57.381 --> 00:21:00.134
Guess they just didn't
have anything else handy.

00:21:00.301 --> 00:21:05.306
Since last year's failed launch
of our fifth satellite, Ghida...

00:21:05.431 --> 00:21:07.558
the scope of the program
has been drastically reduced.

00:21:07.641 --> 00:21:10.811
Many voices in the House of
Nobles call for our abolition.

00:21:10.895 --> 00:21:15.065
We've already lost
half our year's budget!

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:20.321
They say the only money we're gonna
get is for tearing down the facilities.

00:21:20.446 --> 00:21:22.323
That's it, then.

00:21:22.448 --> 00:21:25.159
We might as well start
looking for new jobs.

00:21:26.535 --> 00:21:30.498
However... However, gentlemen!
Now's the time to show them all!

00:21:30.581 --> 00:21:33.709
We must show them the significance...

00:21:33.834 --> 00:21:38.547
of mankind setting sail into
the vastness of space.

00:21:39.006 --> 00:21:42.968
How is it a space Wars/up if
it'll only be carrying people?

00:21:44.053 --> 00:21:45.513
That's what the
General's calling it.

00:21:45.679 --> 00:21:49.350
Space is vast! It is out
there that our future lies!

00:21:49.433 --> 00:21:53.521
A peaceful world we
must open to our posterity.

00:21:54.021 --> 00:21:58.025
People? How're they gonna
launch off something that heavy?

00:22:00.402 --> 00:22:01.821
It's impossible.

00:22:01.904 --> 00:22:05.533
I bet it won't even fly out of our sight.

00:22:05.699 --> 00:22:10.538
I have just put in motion the human
race's first manned space program.

00:22:13.541 --> 00:22:15.042
We all gotta die sometime.

00:22:15.167 --> 00:22:17.795
Yes, there have been
martyrs to our cause.

00:22:17.878 --> 00:22:20.714
However, we must carry
on past that sorrow!

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:23.467
Carry on towards
the future!

00:22:23.551 --> 00:22:27.555
I'm here to ask for a volunteer to
be our nation's first space pilot.

00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:29.265
I won't force anyone.

00:22:29.390 --> 00:22:31.725
Is there any brave man among you...

00:22:31.809 --> 00:22:33.811
who would challenge the world
of the stars?!

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:43.320
I volunteer, sir!

00:22:46.532 --> 00:22:48.617
Are you nuts?!

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:56.083
Uh, ahh...
And you are...?

00:22:56.208 --> 00:22:59.044
Shirotsugh, sir!
Shirotsugh Lhadatt, sir!

00:22:59.712 --> 00:23:03.883
Ah yes, I remember now.
Uh, anybody else?

00:23:05.759 --> 00:23:09.263
Very well then.
I'm pleased you've volunteered.

00:23:09.346 --> 00:23:11.515
Come to the conference
room later on.

00:23:11.599 --> 00:23:13.434
anybody- - -?

00:23:13.517 --> 00:23:15.060
Never mind.

00:23:15.769 --> 00:23:16.896
Dismissed!

00:23:17.396 --> 00:23:19.607
What did you
do that for?!

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:20.858
- Can you believe this guy?

00:23:20.858 --> 00:23:21.901
- Can you believe this guy?
- Don't get involved!

00:23:22.818 --> 00:23:24.778
Don't do this, please!
Think of your family!

00:23:24.862 --> 00:23:26.906
You're gonna die, man!
You're just gonna die!

00:23:27.114 --> 00:23:30.534
Think about it! How many guys
did we have when we joined?

00:23:31.118 --> 00:23:33.537
It wasn't only us, was it?

00:23:34.038 --> 00:23:38.792
Matti, we're being asked to
give our lives for science.

00:23:39.793 --> 00:23:43.797
We're making history here!
Shouldn't we do the best we can?

00:24:28.676 --> 00:24:32.054
To be honest, I really wasn't
expecting too much from you...

00:24:32.179 --> 00:24:35.975
but you are doing much
better than I thought you would.

00:24:36.350 --> 00:24:38.727
Your grades were just really low before.

00:24:39.812 --> 00:24:42.106
Oh well,
it really doesn't matter.

00:24:42.189 --> 00:24:45.651
At this rate, the project should
really start moving in earnest.

00:24:46.026 --> 00:24:47.861
I'll be leaving for
the capital soon.

00:24:47.987 --> 00:24:49.863
To face the lions in
their den, so to speak.

00:24:49.947 --> 00:24:51.198
I'll be busy...

00:24:51.323 --> 00:24:54.660
but our Force will finally
have its space warship!

00:24:55.035 --> 00:24:57.162
Oh'?
So it'll have guns on it?

00:24:57.621 --> 00:24:59.790
Why would a space warship
need guns?

00:24:59.873 --> 00:25:01.875
This space warship is going to have...

00:25:02.001 --> 00:25:04.128
clever gadgets designed to
keep you alive.

00:25:04.211 --> 00:25:07.172
Although we may have to
skimp on a few of those...

00:25:07.256 --> 00:25:10.009
what else was I
going to tell you...?

00:25:10.092 --> 00:25:12.886
Oh, I've forgotten what I was
going to say! Dismissed!

00:25:13.012 --> 00:25:14.805
Dismissing, sir.

00:25:16.098 --> 00:25:18.642
Ah, wait! Wait, wait, wait!
I just remembered.

00:25:19.018 --> 00:25:21.729
Oh, what was it...?

00:25:24.064 --> 00:25:25.482
Of course! Fly!

00:25:26.900 --> 00:25:31.155
G-force training in an airplane.
You've never flown, have you?

00:25:31.238 --> 00:25:33.240
Where do I get an airplane?

00:25:33.365 --> 00:25:34.825
Borrow one.

00:25:34.908 --> 00:25:36.243
From where?

00:25:36.410 --> 00:25:38.704
You moron... From the
Air Force, where else?!

00:26:22.998 --> 00:26:25.084
Oh, check out
the fancy suit.

00:26:25.626 --> 00:26:27.419
My legs feel like
they're in a vice!

00:26:27.419 --> 00:26:29.671
Is this the parachute?

00:26:30.089 --> 00:26:31.256
What's this thing do?

00:26:31.340 --> 00:26:32.966
Quit messing with it!

00:26:33.092 --> 00:26:34.259
- Whoops. It came off.

00:26:34.259 --> 00:26:36.261
- Whoops. It came off.
- Now, hold on here...!

00:26:37.554 --> 00:26:38.680
Hey!

00:26:40.516 --> 00:26:41.892
Yeah, yeah.

00:26:46.647 --> 00:26:47.981
Not there. Front!

00:26:48.107 --> 00:26:49.817
Oh. Of course.

00:27:22.057 --> 00:27:26.979
<i>Greto 32, clear for takeoff!
You are clear for takeoff!</i>

00:29:28.350 --> 00:29:29.518
They're back.

00:29:37.776 --> 00:29:39.403
You Okay?

00:29:39.653 --> 00:29:42.531
- You don't look so hot.
- I think I'm gonna throw up.

00:29:42.698 --> 00:29:46.368
What's wrong?
Did he eat something bad?

00:29:46.493 --> 00:29:48.996
And after he came
so far to play, too.

00:29:51.164 --> 00:29:53.333
Hey, wait. Matti!

00:29:53.583 --> 00:29:57.212
Hey...
Did you say <i>play?</i>

00:29:57.337 --> 00:29:58.297
What about it?

00:30:03.051 --> 00:30:03.844
It's work!

00:30:04.344 --> 00:30:09.391
So, there's someone up in
space for you guys to fight?

00:30:10.517 --> 00:30:13.312
Well, just tell us if you find
any enemy aliens out there.

00:30:13.395 --> 00:30:14.563
So we can shoot 'em down!

00:30:17.858 --> 00:30:20.777
Hey, hey. Let's have
a little respect here.

00:30:20.861 --> 00:30:24.698
Those two assholes happen to be a
Lt. colonel and a major, you know.

00:30:24.823 --> 00:30:29.703
Oh?! You guys are officers?
How terribly rude of me!

00:30:29.828 --> 00:30:33.040
I thought those medals were
some kids' toys!

00:30:37.502 --> 00:30:40.213
Why, you little...

00:30:52.851 --> 00:30:56.188
Guys, I can't... I really don't
think I can handle this.

00:31:02.361 --> 00:31:05.322
Wait a minute.
Wait...please.

00:31:05.739 --> 00:31:07.449
You'll be sorry...!!!

00:31:28.428 --> 00:31:31.765
Bad mood, Matti? It's all
over town, practically.

00:31:31.848 --> 00:31:34.851
How you got your ass royally
kicked by some sergeant.

00:31:35.602 --> 00:31:39.106
If you're gonna fight anyone,
make sure it's an officer!

00:31:39.272 --> 00:31:40.524
He didn't beat me!

00:31:40.607 --> 00:31:42.317
Did you get him good?

00:31:42.442 --> 00:31:44.403
I took it easy on him.

00:31:44.486 --> 00:31:45.278
- It was all your fault!

00:31:45.278 --> 00:31:46.738
- It was all your fault!
- Ow!

00:31:47.239 --> 00:31:51.451
Okay, you two. This here is the
Space Force's secret factory.

00:31:51.743 --> 00:31:54.413
You're gonna love this,
I promise.

00:32:07.467 --> 00:32:11.471
Oh, this is great!
This is incredible!

00:32:11.596 --> 00:32:15.976
Those Air Force guys would shit
themselves if they saw this!

00:32:16.101 --> 00:32:20.147
Right, that's it then.
We'll send you up in this monster.

00:32:20.230 --> 00:32:22.649
Go and die!
Go and die with a BANG!!

00:32:23.316 --> 00:32:25.152
This is the
Space Travel Society...?

00:32:25.527 --> 00:32:28.071
Yeah, they've been at
this for a while now.

00:32:28.155 --> 00:32:31.324
What'?! You're telling me
those old farts did all this?

00:32:33.034 --> 00:32:35.162
Old farts?
Old farts, huh?

00:32:39.791 --> 00:32:42.836
Well, what does that make you,
you little shit?!

00:32:42.919 --> 00:32:46.339
This is Dr. Gnomm. He's just
returned from the North Pole.

00:32:46.465 --> 00:32:48.008
I was flying rockets...

00:32:48.133 --> 00:32:51.511
before you were even an
itch in your daddy's crotch!

00:32:52.929 --> 00:32:55.682
The Doc's a pioneer in
engine nozzle design.

00:33:01.688 --> 00:33:03.690
Would all personnel
assemble, please?

00:33:04.858 --> 00:33:07.944
I've found a problem.
A serious flaw in these plans.

00:33:24.961 --> 00:33:26.296
Well?! Let's have it!

00:33:26.713 --> 00:33:30.926
It's the third stage. I hear you're
putting a hydrogen engine in there.

00:33:31.384 --> 00:33:33.553
Since when do we actually
have a working model?

00:33:33.720 --> 00:33:37.557
Well, we don't, yet. But there's
a first time for everything.

00:33:38.391 --> 00:33:41.061
You can't run an engine
test using this plan!

00:33:41.520 --> 00:33:43.897
We feel a hydrogen engine
would work best...

00:33:43.980 --> 00:33:46.066
for the third stage's
acceleration.

00:33:46.358 --> 00:33:47.567
It's rash!

00:33:47.651 --> 00:33:52.280
Quiet! You don't know what you're
talking about! Quit complaining!

00:33:52.405 --> 00:33:55.116
He's the one who's gonna fly it.
He should decide.

00:33:55.242 --> 00:33:57.244
Oh, and what does
he know about it?

00:33:57.327 --> 00:34:00.288
Just that I'm for the safest way.
I don't wanna die this young.

00:34:00.413 --> 00:34:02.791
Ah, youth!
Youth is overrated!

00:34:02.916 --> 00:34:04.584
It shouldn't be underrated!

00:34:04.709 --> 00:34:08.088
What, then? We can't redesign
anything below the third stage.

00:34:08.421 --> 00:34:12.092
Everything from here to the head
of section four is outmoded design.

00:34:12.175 --> 00:34:14.469
I can show you how to
reduce construction weight...

00:34:14.594 --> 00:34:16.596
and improve the engines'
combustion efficiency.

00:34:16.721 --> 00:34:18.348
When could you
have it all ready?

00:34:18.431 --> 00:34:19.849
Next month.

00:34:19.933 --> 00:34:21.560
When next month'?

00:34:21.643 --> 00:34:22.978
The fourth of Poh.

00:34:23.562 --> 00:34:27.607
Fine, we'll wait till then.
But not any longer than that.

00:34:27.732 --> 00:34:30.652
That's it!
Everyone back to work!

00:34:34.823 --> 00:34:39.035
You throw a rock. It falls to
the ground. That's common sense.

00:34:39.119 --> 00:34:42.914
Now throw that rock really hard,
towards the horizon...

00:34:43.999 --> 00:34:46.459
and it falls to the
ground really far away.

00:34:46.793 --> 00:34:49.504
Keep throwing your rock
harder and harder...

00:34:49.629 --> 00:34:52.215
and it'll eventually
reach a speed where...

00:34:52.340 --> 00:34:56.219
it falls towards the
horizon without ever landing.

00:34:56.803 --> 00:34:59.472
What you have then is
an artificial satellite.

00:34:59.848 --> 00:35:01.182
Instead of
continuing to rise...

00:35:01.308 --> 00:35:04.519
it falls along the
curve of Earth.

00:35:04.644 --> 00:35:07.981
Since the atmosphere would keep
you from maintaining this speed...

00:35:08.064 --> 00:35:10.442
you have to fly way up high
and actually get out of it.

00:35:10.817 --> 00:35:14.154
When it's time to land, you simply
skim the atmosphere and slow down.

00:35:14.237 --> 00:35:17.782
Just a moment's deceleration
and back you fall to the ground.

00:35:17.949 --> 00:35:22.120
In short, we're working day and night
to build this state-of-the-art machine...

00:35:22.203 --> 00:35:24.497
designed to go up
just so it can come down again.

00:35:24.623 --> 00:35:26.791
The description makes it
sound ridiculously simple...

00:35:26.875 --> 00:35:30.629
but I think I like
its basic simplicity.

00:35:32.380 --> 00:35:34.549
These old guys and their
"Space Travel Society"...

00:35:35.634 --> 00:35:38.178
they can't talk
straight about anything.

00:35:38.803 --> 00:35:42.265
Doc Gnomm though...
He's different.

00:35:42.932 --> 00:35:45.560
Of all these old men,
he's the only one you can talk to.

00:35:46.561 --> 00:35:49.648
I don't know what
we'd do without him.

00:35:50.440 --> 00:35:54.944
Torom, Marhida, Gana, Moraa...
My mighty adventurers.

00:35:55.153 --> 00:35:56.321
They're machines.

00:35:56.321 --> 00:35:58.198
Oh, now what?!

00:35:58.281 --> 00:36:02.035
Making fun of manufacturing?
It brought equality to...

00:36:02.160 --> 00:36:05.497
the masses by increasing
the distribution of property!

00:36:05.705 --> 00:36:07.165
Where are the names from?

00:36:07.248 --> 00:36:10.251
Torom's a fish that lives in
the Eska Sea, just below the equator.

00:36:10.627 --> 00:36:12.921
Marhida is a man-eating
whale from the North Sea.

00:36:13.046 --> 00:36:15.215
Gana is a poisonous snake
from the Yvsak River.

00:36:15.340 --> 00:36:16.508
Ready!

00:36:16.591 --> 00:36:17.717
Right!

00:36:17.801 --> 00:36:19.928
All of them were
once deadly enemies.

00:36:20.053 --> 00:36:22.472
But now they're my sons.

00:36:23.640 --> 00:36:25.308
Oh. I thought they
were girls' names.

00:36:25.392 --> 00:36:27.560
There're a few of those, too.

00:36:29.896 --> 00:36:31.773
And now Dhotonridl is born.

00:36:32.524 --> 00:36:35.777
Since I'm in charge of
the parts, I name them all.

00:36:36.236 --> 00:36:40.573
Looks like the only part around
here I didn't name is you.

00:37:04.681 --> 00:37:07.517
Who...
Who's there?

00:37:08.059 --> 00:37:11.271
"The Prince of Space
has come to pay a call."

00:37:11.730 --> 00:37:13.773
Oh, Shirotsugh...!

00:37:24.576 --> 00:37:25.785
Good evening!

00:37:26.327 --> 00:37:28.037
Good evening, Shirotsugh.

00:37:28.455 --> 00:37:30.707
Hey, what gives?
Why's it so dark in there?

00:37:30.832 --> 00:37:32.667
They've turned my power off.

00:37:32.792 --> 00:37:34.627
What'?! That's terrible!

00:37:34.794 --> 00:37:38.298
It's all right, though.
Candlelight is really pretty.

00:37:38.423 --> 00:37:41.301
And Manna's making all sorts of
interestingly shaped candles, too.

00:37:42.927 --> 00:37:46.347
Say, can you come out'?
The sky's full of stars tonight.

00:37:48.641 --> 00:37:51.561
I can tell you about the stars,
like you asked me to.

00:37:51.811 --> 00:37:53.146
Just a sec.

00:37:57.150 --> 00:37:59.611
Come on, Manna. Let's go
out and look at the stars!

00:38:06.993 --> 00:38:09.329
Now then, you see the
prow star up there?

00:38:09.454 --> 00:38:12.999
It's 70 years away
at the speed of light.

00:38:14.083 --> 00:38:17.504
The light we're seeing now
left that star 70 years ago.

00:38:17.587 --> 00:38:20.215
So if we were 70 years old,
then the light produced...

00:38:20.340 --> 00:38:23.468
on my birthday would
just be getting here now.

00:38:24.010 --> 00:38:25.220
Stars!

00:38:25.678 --> 00:38:27.680
Uh, yeah. That's right.

00:38:27.931 --> 00:38:33.019
I wonder what our world must look like,
from out among the stars...

00:38:33.228 --> 00:38:36.022
Oh yeah! I've got
something to show you.

00:38:36.356 --> 00:38:38.983
It's a satellite
photo of our world.

00:38:43.822 --> 00:38:44.989
It's black.

00:38:45.532 --> 00:38:47.951
No, no.
The white part is the ground.

00:38:48.034 --> 00:38:50.870
It's a radar image,
so the picture's not very clear.

00:38:51.371 --> 00:38:53.957
Still, from that far away...

00:38:54.040 --> 00:38:56.918
our city lights would
probably look like stars.

00:38:58.211 --> 00:39:00.338
The fires of our wars, as well.

00:39:00.880 --> 00:39:03.758
They're too sinful...

00:39:03.883 --> 00:39:06.678
to be mixing among
the pure light of the stars...

00:40:27.008 --> 00:40:27.926
Salute!

00:40:48.112 --> 00:40:50.239
A Holy Book?
But,

00:40:50.823 --> 00:40:54.077
I know, but I still
want you to have it.

00:40:54.160 --> 00:40:57.413
Something to read if you ever
feel troubled by anything.

00:40:57.497 --> 00:41:02.335
Well, I'd rather you were
with me when I read it.

00:41:08.341 --> 00:41:09.968
Let's make some tea.

00:41:10.343 --> 00:41:11.344
Manna.

00:41:14.681 --> 00:41:17.642
You don't let yourself
have any fun, do you?

00:41:17.725 --> 00:41:20.895
Can't you and God work out
some sort of a compromise?

00:41:21.020 --> 00:41:22.438
Compromise?!

00:41:23.481 --> 00:41:25.274
I mean, don't overdo it.

00:41:25.358 --> 00:41:27.527
I don't think I'm overdoing anything!

00:41:27.610 --> 00:41:30.238
And that, that "compromise"
you're talking about...

00:41:30.363 --> 00:41:32.407
is what's made the
world what it is today!

00:41:32.532 --> 00:41:34.784
It's become a lot easier to live in.

00:41:40.206 --> 00:41:42.875
Manna! I said we
were making tea now!

00:41:47.880 --> 00:41:51.050
Oh, what's wrong?
We weren't fighting.

00:41:51.134 --> 00:41:55.555
Forgive me.
See, we've made up already.

00:41:59.851 --> 00:42:02.520
Voile! A little
present from Papa.

00:42:02.895 --> 00:42:05.481
A real, live
training simulator.

00:42:11.237 --> 00:42:12.488
Me first!

00:42:13.031 --> 00:42:15.366
Wow, this thing's cool.

00:42:15.742 --> 00:42:18.911
85 million radeks, man.
85 million!

00:42:18.995 --> 00:42:20.913
That's a lot of money,
so don't break it.

00:42:21.039 --> 00:42:23.666
Truth is, we really don't have
the money. Things will be...

00:42:23.750 --> 00:42:25.418
a lot better if the Assembly
approves this appropriation.

00:42:25.543 --> 00:42:27.920
Huh? They still
haven't approved it?

00:42:28.004 --> 00:42:30.048
So where're we
getting our money from?

00:42:30.381 --> 00:42:31.507
Oh, here and there.

00:42:32.091 --> 00:42:33.009
Here and there?

00:42:33.718 --> 00:42:35.511
You really don't know?

00:42:37.430 --> 00:42:39.098
Well, being part
of the nobility...

00:42:39.182 --> 00:42:42.268
the General's got a lot
of pull with the royal family.

00:42:42.351 --> 00:42:45.563
So there's this slightly illegal
business he has on the side.

00:42:45.646 --> 00:42:46.606
- With just his one telephone?

00:42:46.606 --> 00:42:48.775
- With just his one telephone?
- One phone's all he needs.

00:42:48.858 --> 00:42:51.110
No one's there to take calls.
You see, from this year on...

00:42:51.194 --> 00:42:53.821
the royal family buys its
business cars from Miguren Motors.

00:42:53.946 --> 00:42:56.908
The same Miguren Motors
that's paying for our rocket.

00:42:58.284 --> 00:42:59.786
That's how it all works.

00:42:59.911 --> 00:43:02.288
Oh, sure.
That's how it all works.

00:43:02.789 --> 00:43:04.415
You're totally lost,
aren't you?

00:43:04.499 --> 00:43:05.625
Idiot!

00:43:21.140 --> 00:43:25.061
I'm here today to announce the
Space Force High Command's plans...

00:43:25.144 --> 00:43:29.816
for the construction of
our nation's space warship!

00:43:31.484 --> 00:43:34.529
<i>That was the only statement
the Space Force's commander made.</i>

00:43:34.654 --> 00:43:37.490
<i>Also present at the ceremony was
his Royal Highness Prince Toness...</i>

00:43:37.615 --> 00:43:39.784
<i>who briefly addressed the crowd.</i>

00:43:40.034 --> 00:43:44.163
<i>As the protector
of the citizenry...</i>

00:43:44.288 --> 00:43:49.001
<i>of the Honneamano-Jikein-
Minadhan Federated Kingdom...</i>

00:43:49.085 --> 00:43:51.129
Don't stand there!

00:43:53.005 --> 00:43:54.090
There, it's back.

00:43:54.173 --> 00:43:55.800
You're such a hick!

00:44:00.680 --> 00:44:04.809
<i>The most important equipment
in that spacecraft is you.</i>

00:44:05.101 --> 00:44:07.019
<i>Air, water, heat...</i>

00:44:07.145 --> 00:44:08.813
<i>they will provide you with
conditions which differ...</i>

00:44:08.896 --> 00:44:11.774
<i>not in the slightest from
the room you sleep in at night.</i>

00:44:12.316 --> 00:44:15.695
In return, you give it
the proper instructions.

00:44:15.820 --> 00:44:18.197
That's your relationship
with it in a nutshell.

00:44:18.281 --> 00:44:19.991
<i>Trying to muscle it around
won't do you any good.</i>

00:44:20.074 --> 00:44:22.285
<i>Move calmly,
as a pan' of the machine.</i>

00:44:22.535 --> 00:44:25.288
<i>As delicately as possible,
as intimately as possible...</i>

00:44:26.497 --> 00:44:33.254
6000, 6500, 7000, 7500.
Second stage ignition.

00:44:35.631 --> 00:44:36.716
Normal!

00:44:36.799 --> 00:44:39.719
<i>8000, 8500.</i>

00:44:40.219 --> 00:44:41.220
9000, 9500!

00:44:47.727 --> 00:44:50.479
Space Force Headquarters.
...Yeah.

00:44:54.233 --> 00:44:56.485
Phone call.
It's a girl.

00:45:07.246 --> 00:45:09.081
Yes, yes. Hello?

00:45:09.165 --> 00:45:12.752
<i>Shirotsugh? For God's sake,
get out here fast! Help me!</i>

00:45:27.266 --> 00:45:29.602
Hey, what do you think?
I just finished.

00:45:29.685 --> 00:45:31.646
Pretty slick, huh?
Wanna take her for a spin?

00:45:31.771 --> 00:45:34.732
Great, you're gonna try it!
I changed the ignition switch.

00:45:34.815 --> 00:45:37.151
What do you think?
Runs pretty good, huh?

00:45:40.238 --> 00:45:42.406
Space Rider! Cool!

00:46:42.216 --> 00:46:45.803
The men from the power company
kept coming, day after day...

00:46:46.512 --> 00:46:51.058
The house belonged to my aunt,
so I thought everything was okay.

00:46:51.183 --> 00:46:52.810
But the men...

00:46:53.519 --> 00:46:56.314
My aunt owed people money.

00:46:56.981 --> 00:47:01.068
So? So'?! That doesn't
make what they did r/Qqhz'!

00:47:06.490 --> 00:47:08.200
Power plant...?

00:47:09.702 --> 00:47:13.748
Right, we'll take 'em to court!
The state will pay for the lawsuit.

00:47:14.332 --> 00:47:17.209
Or I will, if you want.
If you need a lawyer...

00:47:17.293 --> 00:47:20.296
No, it's all right.
Really, it's all right.

00:47:21.047 --> 00:47:24.091
I don't want her to
see any more fighting.

00:47:24.216 --> 00:47:27.386
Her parents were like that.

00:47:28.596 --> 00:47:29.722
Just fighting, day after day.

00:47:30.014 --> 00:47:32.308
Stop it!
Stop it, please!

00:47:34.769 --> 00:47:38.522
I'm sorry I called you out
here for something like this.

00:47:39.106 --> 00:47:42.818
Something like this?
But it's... It's...

00:47:44.153 --> 00:47:46.655
There's a church
not far from here.

00:47:46.739 --> 00:47:50.201
There are people
there who will help.

00:47:50.576 --> 00:47:53.954
I think I can stay with
them for a little while.

00:47:54.497 --> 00:47:57.833
And Manna can make some
friends there, too...

00:48:00.211 --> 00:48:01.337
All right...

00:48:02.963 --> 00:48:05.383
Come on,
let's dig your stuff out.

00:48:05.841 --> 00:48:10.763
<i>...splendor is most evident in the
famous Nedens Palace. This beauty...</i>

00:48:12.932 --> 00:48:15.476
<i>...regi0n, today will be fine...</i>

00:48:15.601 --> 00:48:17.561
<i>with clouds moving
in later tonight...</i>

00:48:25.236 --> 00:48:28.447
"The Age of Fire.
When God created man..."

00:48:28.656 --> 00:48:33.411
"man was like the animals
and did not possess fire."

00:48:34.453 --> 00:48:36.872
"It is with fire that
God lives forever."

00:48:36.956 --> 00:48:41.669
"Dao stole a burning branch
and ran off as fast as he could."

00:48:41.961 --> 00:48:45.214
"But the Protector of the
ovens had foreseen this..."

00:48:45.297 --> 00:48:48.008
"and had cursed the fire."

00:48:48.717 --> 00:48:52.847
"Dao carried the fire home, and
tried to use it like God himself."

00:48:52.972 --> 00:48:55.641
"And Dads seven sons were killed."

00:48:56.559 --> 00:48:59.437
"These were mankind's
first deaths."

00:49:00.020 --> 00:49:03.566
"And God appeared before
Dao and gave a prophecy."

00:49:04.066 --> 00:49:07.528
" 'Man,' he said,
'you have been cursed.' "

00:49:07.653 --> 00:49:11.824
" 'Your children shall struggle
and quarrel and live in sorrow.' "

00:49:12.324 --> 00:49:15.161
" 'Their misfortune shall spread
to the ends of the land.' "

00:49:15.286 --> 00:49:17.955
" 'They shall murder one another
until the end of time.' "

00:49:21.667 --> 00:49:25.087
You're sure it's safe
standing this close?

00:49:25.171 --> 00:49:27.840
Ah, we're fine, we're fine.

00:49:28.549 --> 00:49:32.511
The old engines would blow
every time we throttled up!

00:49:33.095 --> 00:49:37.892
It took 20 years to get to this state.
Sorta like real sons.

00:49:39.018 --> 00:49:41.437
Insolent, and a real pain
in the ass sometimes!

00:49:41.604 --> 00:49:44.857
You can tell kids are in a bad mood
when they don't eat breakfast!

00:49:44.982 --> 00:49:47.067
Yeah! Even when they
turn on their old man...

00:49:47.193 --> 00:49:50.488
they don't do it all of a sudden.
They'll give some warning first.

00:50:18.098 --> 00:50:20.392
1,4,5.

00:50:20.601 --> 00:50:23.687
<i>1...4...5.</i>

00:50:28.817 --> 00:50:31.153
So, you weren't
hit by any fragments?

00:50:31.403 --> 00:50:32.696
Not even a piece.

00:50:32.947 --> 00:50:35.241
Oh sure, you get
away safe and sound...

00:50:35.324 --> 00:50:37.701
and the Doc winds
up in the hospital.

00:50:40.204 --> 00:50:42.373
Serves him right,
leaving me there like that.

00:50:42.456 --> 00:50:43.707
Next one's 5, 6.

00:50:43.791 --> 00:50:45.668
5, 6.
Well, thanks to this...

00:50:45.751 --> 00:50:47.378
getting in and out of the
factory's gotten complicated.

00:50:47.461 --> 00:50:49.421
1, 3, 4.
Why's that?

00:50:50.005 --> 00:50:52.925
Because they think the
radicals may have done it.

00:50:53.259 --> 00:50:54.552
Radicals?

00:50:54.802 --> 00:50:57.680
The guys who oppose
the King's decisions.

00:50:57.763 --> 00:51:00.349
There've been a lot of
protest letters lately.

00:51:00.432 --> 00:51:01.642
News to me.

00:51:01.767 --> 00:51:04.562
They're burning them
day after day.

00:51:04.645 --> 00:51:08.148
And now some idiots are actually
yelling for random bombings.

00:51:08.899 --> 00:51:09.942
Next.

00:51:10.526 --> 00:51:12.403
<i>Uhh...
3, 4, 5.</i>

00:51:12.945 --> 00:51:16.198
What? Gimme that.

00:51:16.615 --> 00:51:19.451
Hey, that's the second row!

00:51:21.370 --> 00:51:23.289
For crying out loud...

00:51:23.414 --> 00:51:24.540
Sorry.

00:51:24.623 --> 00:51:27.459
Better get with it,
or else it won't work...

00:51:27.543 --> 00:51:31.463
Hey, someone get the cat and his
keeper off the electronic brain!

00:51:32.131 --> 00:51:33.507
Don't you have a job'?

00:51:33.882 --> 00:51:38.554
Pulled an all-nighter last night.
The old guys were at it again...

00:51:42.099 --> 00:51:43.309
Quit shakin' it!

00:51:43.726 --> 00:51:46.228
The Doc, he's...
He's dead!

00:51:46.353 --> 00:51:47.313
When?!

00:51:47.438 --> 00:51:49.940
A little while ago,
at the hospital.

00:53:19.697 --> 00:53:21.865
<i>The Space Force's gala
promotional reception...</i>

00:53:21.949 --> 00:53:24.493
<i>Welcomed a royal
guest from the capital.</i>

00:53:24.576 --> 00:53:28.247
<i>Also appearing tonight was
the world's first astronaut...</i>

00:53:28.330 --> 00:53:30.332
<i>Lt. Colonel
Shirotsugh Lhadatt.</i>

00:53:30.416 --> 00:53:32.751
<i>That dress uniform he's
wearing really suits him.</i>

00:53:32.835 --> 00:53:36.171
<i>When Prince Toness asked, "Doesn't
going into space frighten you?"...</i>

00:53:36.422 --> 00:53:41.677
<i>he lightheartedly replied,
"It really hasn't bothered me."</i>

00:53:46.640 --> 00:53:50.769
You in there! Have you ever
had to worry about money?

00:53:50.853 --> 00:53:55.816
You have no idea what it's like!
We don't even have a urinal to piss in!

00:53:55.941 --> 00:53:58.569
It's getting colder
and colder for us.

00:53:58.652 --> 00:54:02.614
You think you can survive winter
with only two blankets?

00:54:06.076 --> 00:54:07.619
Outta the way!
Lemme through!

00:54:07.745 --> 00:54:09.288
What good does an astronaut do?

00:54:09.413 --> 00:54:11.415
Look at the bridges we built...

00:54:14.960 --> 00:54:17.796
What's with these
guys out front?

00:54:17.921 --> 00:54:19.882
Protest. It was
hell this morning.

00:54:19.965 --> 00:54:22.801
The protesters were fighting
against the beggars over the place.

00:54:22.885 --> 00:54:25.179
So what's the unemployment
movement want with us?

00:54:25.304 --> 00:54:27.473
No, no.
It's the anti-war movement.

00:54:27.598 --> 00:54:30.058
They're saying we should be
building bridges and not rockets.

00:54:30.142 --> 00:54:32.811
Like I said,
the unemployment movement!

00:54:32.895 --> 00:54:35.647
Spend all our money for a bunch
of bridges we don't need, huh?

00:54:35.731 --> 00:54:39.318
Out in the country, we still
use boats, for God's sake!

00:54:39.443 --> 00:54:42.029
I'd take the bridges
over a space warship.

00:54:43.572 --> 00:54:45.449
At least those
wouldn't kill anyone.

00:54:48.243 --> 00:54:50.579
Hey, hey, hey,
don't let 'em get to you.

00:54:50.662 --> 00:54:53.373
They're just saying all
that because they want jobs.

00:54:53.624 --> 00:54:56.043
This rocket will
be used for war.

00:54:57.127 --> 00:54:59.671
You can use
bridges for war, too.

00:55:01.340 --> 00:55:04.301
You're the one
who started all this!

00:55:04.510 --> 00:55:07.012
Me'?
I doubt that.

00:55:07.888 --> 00:55:10.057
Then who started it?

00:55:10.724 --> 00:55:11.767
Hey!

00:55:27.699 --> 00:55:31.495
<i>Ll'. Colonel Lhadaffis' morning begins
with a glass of fruit juice.</i>

00:55:32.079 --> 00:55:34.456
<i>After light training,
he eats a hearty breakfast...</i>

00:55:34.540 --> 00:55:38.001
<i>of soft bread
and broiled kress fruit.</i>

00:55:38.335 --> 00:55:40.838
<i>Right, because
they're good for you.</i>

00:55:40.921 --> 00:55:43.215
<i>Shirotsugh Lhadatt,
ladies and gentlemen.</i>

00:56:24.590 --> 00:56:25.424
Wham?!

00:56:26.925 --> 00:56:28.302
Asshole!

00:56:39.229 --> 00:56:40.898
Hey! Yo!

00:56:46.486 --> 00:56:47.654
Matti! You...!

00:56:47.779 --> 00:56:50.115
Good, there you are.
I was just reading the paper...

00:56:50.198 --> 00:56:53.243
Oh? You're wet.
We've got trouble!

00:56:58.290 --> 00:57:00.626
It says here that the
launch will be from Kanea.

00:57:01.376 --> 00:57:04.963
When was the launch
site moved so far south?

00:57:05.297 --> 00:57:06.965
Oh, didn't you know?

00:57:07.090 --> 00:57:10.469
We can't use the Army's
launch site after all.

00:57:12.471 --> 00:57:15.557
600 ren west of Kanea?!
That's over the border!

00:57:17.351 --> 00:57:21.188
No, it's all right.
Ah, there's a map...

00:57:31.657 --> 00:57:33.742
It's right on the
demilitarized zone!

00:57:34.576 --> 00:57:38.872
No, no. This way it's
3000 ren closer to the equator.

00:57:38.997 --> 00:57:42.250
It'll be easier to make
it to orbit, you see...

00:57:42.501 --> 00:57:46.463
Yeah, I know!
My God, how could they?

00:57:46.546 --> 00:57:48.423
They're sending us
to a powder keg...

00:57:48.507 --> 00:57:51.551
to launch off the world's
biggest firecracker!

00:57:51.677 --> 00:57:54.346
Wasn't anyone against it'?!

00:57:54.429 --> 00:57:57.265
It wasn't our decision.
It was the ministry's.

00:57:57.391 --> 00:58:01.353
Ministry? What minis...?
The Defense Ministry'?!

00:58:13.949 --> 00:58:18.620
<i>...norinosska, zuiben mattoishi
suru rekujishieto.</i>

00:58:19.037 --> 00:58:23.250
<i>Uh, kurufateeji onla
Iaku. ..Iakure...</i>

00:58:24.001 --> 00:58:25.877
<i>Lakuretoria!</i>

00:58:26.003 --> 00:58:29.256
Just speak in the
vernacular. Be yourself.

00:58:29.798 --> 00:58:32.551
Thanks, I appreciate it.

00:58:33.343 --> 00:58:36.471
But really, there's
nothing more for me to say.

00:58:40.392 --> 00:58:43.520
You're finished?
Then let me speak.

00:58:43.812 --> 00:58:48.775
You are right, we just don't
see the appeal of your rocket.

00:58:49.526 --> 00:58:53.739
Space travel? We're concerned
with the military here.

00:58:53.864 --> 00:58:56.908
Who would invest in something
that just flies into space?

00:58:57.034 --> 00:59:00.704
It's a waste to assign a whole
squadron to it.

00:59:00.787 --> 00:59:03.957
There's something wrong with the
very existence of the Space Force!

00:59:04.458 --> 00:59:09.212
Well...but...then why let
the project get this far...?

00:59:09.296 --> 00:59:12.424
We needed to find a way
to properly end the program.

00:59:12.507 --> 00:59:15.218
The royal family,
the Transportation Ministry...

00:59:15.302 --> 00:59:17.471
the roots of your Space Force
reach into many areas.

00:59:17.596 --> 00:59:20.515
And all of us finished
regretting a long time ago.

00:59:20.599 --> 00:59:24.061
The only problem now is
how to forget about it.

00:59:24.269 --> 00:59:26.646
We can't just end it by saying,
"Oh, it was useless."

00:59:26.772 --> 00:59:31.443
But, this project is attracting
the attention of every nation.

00:59:31.526 --> 00:59:34.905
Even the Republic wants
our rocket information.

00:59:34.988 --> 00:59:38.408
So, to launch it right on the
border of enemy occupied Rimada...

00:59:38.492 --> 00:59:41.995
So go ahead! Launch it,
or whatever you please.

00:59:42.120 --> 00:59:45.123
We just want for it to be seen by
the Republic's forces in Rimada.

00:59:45.248 --> 00:59:48.502
And what will they do with a lovely
rocket right before their eyes?

00:59:48.627 --> 00:59:49.628
Steal it!

00:59:49.711 --> 00:59:54.299
Steal it. That way, it will
at least be useful.

00:59:54.424 --> 00:59:56.635
A border violation
via military force.

00:59:56.760 --> 00:59:59.805
Outright theft of property...
It'll be quite a loss.

00:59:59.888 --> 01:00:02.641
Reparations will have to come
from somewhere, of course.

01:00:02.849 --> 01:00:06.978
The only real question is whether
or not they'll actually attack.

01:00:07.896 --> 01:00:09.064
Don't worry.

01:00:09.147 --> 01:00:13.860
They've quite an investment in
your rocket over there as well, huh?

01:00:19.866 --> 01:00:20.992
- <i>Ready?</i>

01:00:20.992 --> 01:00:21.827
<i>- Ready?
- Ave. Sm!</i>

01:00:21.910 --> 01:00:24.871
<i>We begin. You're cruising along,
about to take a well deserved shit.</i>

01:00:24.996 --> 01:00:30.001
<i>Your altitude is 3000,
speed of 200 ren per second.</i>

01:00:30.418 --> 01:00:35.382
The next contact zone
is far over the horizon.

01:00:38.343 --> 01:00:40.804
Cabin pressure abnormality
in oxygen tank #1!

01:00:40.887 --> 01:00:43.431
Primary lines, closed.
Activating auxiliary power.

01:00:43.515 --> 01:00:46.643
Three!
Suspending nitrogen supply!

01:00:46.768 --> 01:00:49.938
Inertial systems reading
abnormal acceleration.

01:00:50.021 --> 01:00:54.943
Resetting multifunction systems.
Capsule pressure, unchanged!

01:00:56.778 --> 01:00:59.865
Good, you've
earned your paycheck.

01:01:00.157 --> 01:01:02.826
<i>Next, crisis
situation #5- 7-5.</i>

01:01:04.828 --> 01:01:06.621
"The City of Fire."

01:01:06.705 --> 01:01:11.710
"My son, soon you must
depart the marketplace."

01:01:12.544 --> 01:01:15.839
"Here, all the good things
are stained with blood."

01:01:15.922 --> 01:01:19.134
"God will be
silent no longer."

01:01:19.926 --> 01:01:22.554
"This city of filth
was created by fire."

01:01:22.637 --> 01:01:27.058
"By fire it shall
be destroyed."

01:01:28.476 --> 01:01:33.106
"Anything arising from evil will
never be good."

01:01:33.315 --> 01:01:39.196
"And so, my son,
even you must be prepared."

01:02:00.967 --> 01:02:01.760
Stop!

01:02:02.719 --> 01:02:06.640
Calm down, dammit!
You little...!

01:02:15.732 --> 01:02:18.109
Yes, that's perfect.

01:02:20.612 --> 01:02:23.448
Okay, let's have you
lean to the left this time.

01:02:24.532 --> 01:02:28.119
Smile now.
A little more!

01:02:28.286 --> 01:02:29.621
That's it!

01:02:29.746 --> 01:02:33.250
That's the way, nice and cheerful.
A real hero for all the kiddies.

01:02:33.667 --> 01:02:42.217
Shirotsugh!
Shirotsugh! Shirotsugh!

01:03:26.011 --> 01:03:28.013
You're kidding!

01:03:39.024 --> 01:03:41.359
<i>To everyone in the kingdom,
good morning!</i>

01:03:41.484 --> 01:03:45.947
<i>I'm coming to you from the Space
Force Headquarters in Naghatsumih.</i>

01:03:46.448 --> 01:03:49.826
<i>An area which has known
its share of history.</i>

01:03:49.909 --> 01:03:54.873
<i>This port city is famous for
being the core city for Umon.</i>

01:03:54.956 --> 01:03:59.210
<i>It was here that his Highness
the King lived as a child...</i>

01:03:59.336 --> 01:04:02.797
<i>and this neighborhood is famous
for its ties to the royal family.</i>

01:04:02.922 --> 01:04:04.299
<i>The Space Force
Headquarters are...</i>

01:04:04.382 --> 01:04:06.259
Welcome back, General.
When did you get in?

01:04:06.384 --> 01:04:07.093
Last night's train.

01:04:07.218 --> 01:04:09.721
I see. And the
administration's decision?

01:04:09.804 --> 01:04:11.139
No comment!

01:04:12.349 --> 01:04:15.060
You call it a space "warship."
Will it actually carry weaponry?

01:04:15.143 --> 01:04:17.479
No comment!
I can only say that...

01:04:17.562 --> 01:04:20.357
it will be capable
of carrying such devices.

01:04:22.359 --> 01:04:28.573
Can't you look happier?
Like a professional astronaut?

01:04:41.836 --> 01:04:43.880
Lt. Colonel! Lt. Colonel!

01:04:44.047 --> 01:04:47.217
He's been promoted.
It's colonel, now.

01:04:47.425 --> 01:04:50.345
Colonel then.
Smile a bit...smile...

01:04:50.470 --> 01:04:52.222
Got it. Thank you.

01:04:53.431 --> 01:04:55.183
We're about ready to go.

01:04:55.266 --> 01:04:57.602
Cheer up. See you.

01:04:59.646 --> 01:05:03.525
Now, Colonel, be sure to stress
your mission as a space hero.

01:05:04.317 --> 01:05:05.485
Mission?

01:05:06.236 --> 01:05:08.780
Well, you know. The whole
meaning of the space program.

01:05:08.905 --> 01:05:11.533
Why so many people have
died for it so far...

01:05:11.616 --> 01:05:13.993
and why we have to go
on despite all that.

01:05:14.744 --> 01:05:17.038
Just think of
something, okay?

01:05:29.676 --> 01:05:32.470
Look over here,
Mr. Hero. Hey, you!

01:05:33.346 --> 01:05:34.389
Have you heard?

01:05:34.472 --> 01:05:37.684
They say 30,000 people could
have a warm place to live in...

01:05:37.809 --> 01:05:41.229
if the Space Force's
budget were cut by half.

01:05:43.565 --> 01:05:46.025
Well now, any thoughts
on the arms race?

01:05:48.361 --> 01:05:50.238
How about on war?

01:05:50.321 --> 01:05:53.700
You deny the corruption problems
with Miguren Motors?

01:05:54.451 --> 01:05:56.703
You don't know anything, do you?

01:05:56.828 --> 01:06:00.165
Uh, we're about to start! Hey!

01:06:29.527 --> 01:06:33.531
<i>Vice Minister Nerredon of the
Republic today harshly criticized...</i>

01:06:33.865 --> 01:06:38.203
<i>the space warship program
of the Kingdom of Honnéamise...</i>

01:06:38.328 --> 01:06:43.541
<i>calling the entire project
"a threat to world peace."</i>

01:06:51.758 --> 01:06:54.761
Ah, good work this morning.

01:07:02.101 --> 01:07:04.604
The new photographs have arrived, sir.

01:07:04.854 --> 01:07:06.856
The space hero?

01:07:11.694 --> 01:07:15.865
He looks like a presumptuous guy.

01:07:16.866 --> 01:07:20.537
It's almost winter there. The northern
hemisphere's seasons are reversed.

01:07:20.620 --> 01:07:21.746
Ah, I see.

01:07:21.871 --> 01:07:24.374
Lt. Colonel Shirotsugh Lhadatt.

01:07:25.375 --> 01:07:26.876
Doesn't look too bright.

01:07:27.126 --> 01:07:31.130
Weapons Division is urging
we seize the space warship.

01:07:31.631 --> 01:07:34.634
An absurd request. incompetents!

01:07:37.387 --> 01:07:38.763
They'll have to wait.

01:07:38.888 --> 01:07:42.267
Stealing a distant nation's rocket.

01:07:42.392 --> 01:07:45.270
It isn't that simple.

01:07:45.395 --> 01:07:48.898
These things take time to set up.

01:07:51.901 --> 01:07:55.071
The Office of Security is taking
steps to obstruct their progress.

01:07:56.072 --> 01:07:59.075
Assasination... Not terribly subtle, is it?

01:07:59.492 --> 01:08:03.580
But terribly effective, sir.

01:08:12.964 --> 01:08:15.008
" 'Sin is everywhere.' "

01:08:15.133 --> 01:08:17.760
"God said this,
looking down at the world."

01:08:17.844 --> 01:08:22.599
"The sins of man will
immerse the world. We..."

01:08:24.559 --> 01:08:26.144
Shirotsugh!

01:08:40.992 --> 01:08:43.786
Bring in the laundry
before it gets dark.

01:08:44.912 --> 01:08:46.914
Okay?
I'll see you later.

01:09:49.477 --> 01:09:52.397
Nice outfit.
Somebody bought it for you?

01:10:29.851 --> 01:10:31.769
Where's the toilet?

01:11:36.209 --> 01:11:38.336
Manna, bring us some
towels, would you?

01:11:48.179 --> 01:11:49.514
Thank you.

01:11:52.183 --> 01:11:53.059
Thanks.

01:11:53.184 --> 01:11:55.603
Manna, did you bring the
laundry in like I asked you to?

01:11:55.686 --> 01:11:58.314
No one came while
I was out, did they?

01:11:58.397 --> 01:11:59.941
Oh, and if you
see Uncle Dori...

01:12:00.024 --> 01:12:02.610
be sure and thank him
for the winter clothes.

01:12:03.694 --> 01:12:05.988
Even besides that, he's done
so much for us already.

01:13:28.863 --> 01:13:32.909
"You cannot live without
your daily bread."

01:13:33.200 --> 01:13:37.371
"Truth changes to lies
when it leaves your lips."

01:13:37.663 --> 01:13:41.292
"Virtue changes to evil
when it leaves your hands."

01:13:42.501 --> 01:13:46.964
"What you see as good may
not be good as God sees it."

01:13:47.465 --> 01:13:51.427
"What can any of
you do but pray?"

01:13:52.219 --> 01:13:56.349
"Prayer is a small thing,
but it is everything."

01:13:57.725 --> 01:14:00.519
"There is nothing more
noble than prayer."

01:14:00.645 --> 01:14:02.980
"There is nothing
more humble..."

01:16:13.652 --> 01:16:16.322
Oh, good morning,
Shirotsugh.

01:16:17.990 --> 01:16:20.284
It looks like
nice weather today.

01:16:20.409 --> 01:16:22.453
About last night...

01:16:24.455 --> 01:16:27.833
Forgive me. I couldn't...
I was... Please forgive me.

01:16:27.958 --> 01:16:30.377
You didn't do anything.

01:16:30.461 --> 01:16:32.088
Because I couldn't!

01:16:32.588 --> 01:16:35.633
Forgive me. I don't
know what came over me.

01:16:35.716 --> 01:16:38.010
Hitting a wonderful
person like you...

01:16:40.721 --> 01:16:44.016
I didn't mean to.
You aren't hurt, are you?

01:16:44.141 --> 01:16:45.976
What? No!! That's not...

01:16:46.102 --> 01:16:49.313
No, I know you'll
forgive me...

01:16:49.396 --> 01:16:52.525
but I'll never be
able to forgive myself.

01:16:52.650 --> 01:16:54.026
Believe me, I'm sorry.

01:17:07.498 --> 01:17:10.084
Hey, isn't that
Shirotsugh over there?

01:17:10.167 --> 01:17:13.587
That idiot. And wearing
the peacock suit, too!

01:17:15.422 --> 01:17:16.423
Yo!

01:17:17.550 --> 01:17:18.843
Hi!

01:17:18.926 --> 01:17:21.387
Ohh...you idiot! Why'd you
have to wear that thing?

01:17:21.512 --> 01:17:24.390
Don't you know you're
a celebrity around here?

01:17:24.515 --> 01:17:28.310
Dress uniform's the thing to wear
for sending you off to your posts.

01:17:28.894 --> 01:17:32.189
So where'd you disappear
to all of a sudden for three days?

01:17:32.314 --> 01:17:34.859
Were you with
a girl or something?

01:17:34.984 --> 01:17:36.152
<i>Well...</i>

01:17:36.277 --> 01:17:38.779
Why, you little...!

01:17:40.197 --> 01:17:42.074
Tchallichammi! Majaho!

01:17:42.199 --> 01:17:44.785
You are hereby dispatched
to the Guria Observatory.

01:17:45.828 --> 01:17:47.121
Move out!

01:17:48.080 --> 01:17:49.248
Salute!

01:17:51.458 --> 01:17:55.296
Drop us a line when you get into
space. We'll be easy to find.

01:17:55.379 --> 01:17:57.798
And don't make
any more work for us.

01:17:59.758 --> 01:18:01.927
At ease!

01:18:26.118 --> 01:18:29.038
It's gonna be lonely around here
with all you guys leaving.

01:18:29.121 --> 01:18:32.291
Well, Darigan's in charge
of launch control training.

01:18:32.416 --> 01:18:35.127
He and I'll be leaving for the
launch site the day after tomorrow.

01:18:35.252 --> 01:18:37.630
Nekkerout might still be around.

01:18:37.755 --> 01:18:40.257
Hell, Kharock's already gone to
the launch site with the old men.

01:18:40.341 --> 01:18:43.260
I got some mail the other day.
When are you gonne head over there?

01:18:43.385 --> 01:18:46.764
I don't know. OI' Baldy just
won't give me a break.

01:18:46.847 --> 01:18:49.558
Looks like I keep training
right up 'til the end.

01:18:50.851 --> 01:18:51.393
- How much'?

01:18:51.393 --> 01:18:52.978
<i>- How much'?
- 3 gaku.</i>

01:18:53.437 --> 01:18:57.566
Say, Matti... Suppose
that life was a story...

01:18:57.816 --> 01:18:59.443
Come again?

01:18:59.610 --> 01:19:02.112
No, if you were to
think about it like that.

01:19:02.238 --> 01:19:05.616
Well, have you ever wondered if...
If maybe you aren't a good guy?

01:19:05.741 --> 01:19:08.619
That you're one of
the bad guys, instead?

01:19:08.953 --> 01:19:13.332
I guess... It's just...
Only...

01:19:13.332 --> 01:19:16.627
The people around us now,
our parents, everyone.

01:19:16.752 --> 01:19:20.130
You see, I think I'm
here only because...

01:19:20.214 --> 01:19:22.424
they need me even
for a little bit.

01:19:22.508 --> 01:19:24.009
Take this
hardware stand.

01:19:24.134 --> 01:19:27.638
It's here only because
it serves a purpose for someone.

01:19:27.763 --> 01:19:30.724
I don't think there're any totally
useless things in the world.

01:19:30.808 --> 01:19:33.102
How could something
like that exist?

01:19:33.185 --> 01:19:36.313
Someone recognizes this guy's
necessity, so he's here.

01:19:36.397 --> 01:19:38.941
If the need for him were to
disappear, then so would he.

01:19:39.024 --> 01:19:41.527
That's what I think, anyway.
Does it help?

01:19:43.028 --> 01:19:44.989
Yeah, it does. Thanks.

01:20:06.927 --> 01:20:08.512
Run for it!

01:20:10.139 --> 01:20:11.974
Help!

01:21:50.948 --> 01:21:53.117
What's with that old bag?
Is she a radical?

01:21:53.242 --> 01:21:53.951
Like I know?!

01:22:03.877 --> 01:22:05.963
That made me hungry...

01:22:13.971 --> 01:22:16.140
Split up!

01:22:16.223 --> 01:22:18.183
Wait for me Matti!
Wait!

01:22:18.308 --> 01:22:20.060
Get away from me,
you idiot!

01:22:20.185 --> 01:22:21.812
I'm the one
getting shot at!

01:22:21.937 --> 01:22:24.148
Like I said,
get away from me!

01:22:34.950 --> 01:22:36.076
Dead end!

01:22:53.552 --> 01:22:56.972
What the...!
What's going on here?!

01:22:59.433 --> 01:23:01.185
You two okay?

01:23:01.518 --> 01:23:05.731
Hey, look at this!
It's that space guy, Lhadatt!

01:23:07.441 --> 01:23:08.692
Hi...

01:23:18.785 --> 01:23:21.205
We'd better not
go back today.

01:23:21.788 --> 01:23:25.125
Yeah. If she ambushes us again,
we're dead for sure.

01:23:25.334 --> 01:23:27.252
Okay, until you hear
something definite...

01:23:27.377 --> 01:23:29.922
just lose yourself at
that girl's house. See you!

01:23:33.550 --> 01:23:37.012
This is not a jellyfish.
It's a triangular octopus.

01:23:37.054 --> 01:23:38.055
What about this one?

01:23:38.180 --> 01:23:40.557
This? It's a...

01:23:40.974 --> 01:23:41.934
starfish!

01:23:42.059 --> 01:23:43.143
Oh, I see.

01:24:20.597 --> 01:24:22.933
H...Hey! Whoa...!

01:24:23.100 --> 01:24:24.643
Hey, what the...!

01:24:28.772 --> 01:24:31.024
Hey, the hell are you doing!

01:24:40.826 --> 01:24:42.619
Help!!

01:26:22.219 --> 01:26:23.887
You Okay?

01:26:25.639 --> 01:26:27.057
Are you hurt?

01:26:27.140 --> 01:26:28.350
Over here!

01:26:38.318 --> 01:26:39.736
You all right?

01:26:39.820 --> 01:26:41.488
Yeah, fine.

01:26:42.280 --> 01:26:47.494
Civilization did not create war.
War created civilization.

01:26:48.245 --> 01:26:49.621
Who said that?

01:26:49.746 --> 01:26:54.543
I did. The human race broke free
of the hell of primitive times...

01:26:54.626 --> 01:26:57.879
and marched through 100,000 years
to reach this point.

01:26:57.963 --> 01:27:03.093
And what of the present?
Have we really advanced at all?

01:27:03.677 --> 01:27:06.388
When I was young,
I wanted to be a historian.

01:27:06.471 --> 01:27:07.973
Why didn't you'?

01:27:08.140 --> 01:27:12.269
A war started,
so I became a soldier instead.

01:27:12.394 --> 01:27:16.606
I fought desperately to defend my
country from that foreign invasion.

01:27:16.732 --> 01:27:19.234
At the same time, I knew that
it wasn't justice.

01:27:19.317 --> 01:27:22.279
I knew very well that
we were just repeating...

01:27:22.404 --> 01:27:25.115
our murderous past.

01:27:25.198 --> 01:27:27.159
It was quite a blow.

01:27:27.284 --> 01:27:29.244
Not becoming a soldier.

01:27:29.327 --> 01:27:32.205
I mean studying history.

01:27:34.124 --> 01:27:37.753
History is a game which doesn't
end until you've lost everything.

01:27:37.836 --> 01:27:40.964
Perhaps we're not as different from
the monkeys as we like to think.

01:27:41.047 --> 01:27:44.509
Will we repeat our old mistakes?
Do we have any choice in the matter'?

01:27:44.801 --> 01:27:47.679
The most important thing you can do
is to be aware of your situation.

01:27:47.804 --> 01:27:51.475
To ask yourself "What should I do?
What shouldn't I do?"

01:27:51.558 --> 01:27:55.729
The only eyes you can trust are
the ones on top of your own nose.

01:27:55.812 --> 01:27:58.482
Look through them now!
What do they show you?

01:27:58.565 --> 01:27:59.941
A girl's butt.

01:28:00.025 --> 01:28:02.527
You'd miss a forest for the trees.

01:28:21.004 --> 01:28:23.590
Hello, Manna. You're alone?

01:28:24.132 --> 01:28:27.010
Riqunni...must be working.

01:28:27.093 --> 01:28:30.347
Well, could you give
her a message for me'?

01:28:30.472 --> 01:28:35.352
I'll be going away for a while.
I won't be able to visit.

01:28:36.353 --> 01:28:39.481
Manna, would you like me to
bring something back for you?

01:28:39.564 --> 01:28:40.982
A star.

01:28:41.149 --> 01:28:42.943
I can't.

01:28:43.026 --> 01:28:46.196
The stars are really
really far away.

01:28:46.488 --> 01:28:50.450
Tough one... I'm going
where there's nothing at all.

01:28:50.909 --> 01:28:52.244
Out there?

01:28:53.495 --> 01:28:58.250
Yeah, it's out there...
Here, there, and everywhere.

01:29:26.111 --> 01:29:28.238
Oh, Shirotsugh!

01:29:37.289 --> 01:29:38.748
I've gotta go.

01:29:38.874 --> 01:29:40.667
Come back soon.

01:30:12.324 --> 01:30:13.950
Magazine, sir'?

01:30:17.120 --> 01:30:20.290
Uh, Colonel, sir...
May I have your autograph?

01:30:22.292 --> 01:30:23.460
Name'?

01:30:23.543 --> 01:30:26.129
Maashi Treen, sir.

01:30:28.465 --> 01:30:30.133
Thank you, sir.

01:30:31.468 --> 01:30:33.303
Oh, and fasten your seatbelt.

01:31:12.092 --> 01:31:14.594
Wine tasting... Very refined, sir.

01:31:14.844 --> 01:31:17.973
The plan is finally in motion.

01:31:18.056 --> 01:31:18.807
Really?

01:31:19.307 --> 01:31:21.685
We'll be using our forces
stationed in Rimada.

01:31:21.810 --> 01:31:22.477
Jets as well?

01:31:22.560 --> 01:31:26.189
A battlefield test for our latest weapons.

01:31:26.314 --> 01:31:27.315
Excellent.

01:31:41.037 --> 01:31:43.498
Rimadan military trains
are moving north.

01:31:43.581 --> 01:31:45.583
Next report will be at noon.

01:31:46.710 --> 01:31:48.545
So, they're moving.

01:31:48.837 --> 01:31:51.715
Do you think they'll fly
their new jets?

01:31:51.840 --> 01:31:56.928
Yeah, we aren't the only ones
that want to see how well they work.

01:31:57.053 --> 01:32:00.598
With a little luck, we might even
see them do an in-air refueling.

01:32:02.726 --> 01:32:08.148
Hello everyone. This is
astronaut Shirotsugh Lhadatt.

01:32:08.231 --> 01:32:13.611
I am currently in orbit,
flying 200 ren above our world.

01:32:13.737 --> 01:32:15.780
<i>Um...Uhh...</i>

01:32:15.905 --> 01:32:18.491
"What I see now..."

01:32:19.325 --> 01:32:22.620
Oh, I can't do this.

01:32:22.746 --> 01:32:26.458
Umm, "What I see now,
looking down at our world

01:32:26.583 --> 01:32:27.667
Tanks!

01:32:27.751 --> 01:32:30.587
Look again.
They're fakes.

01:32:30.754 --> 01:32:32.130
Fakes?

01:32:32.922 --> 01:32:36.593
"They're fakes, they're fakes.
They're all just fakes..."

01:32:36.718 --> 01:32:38.219
Whoa!

01:32:38.303 --> 01:32:42.557
"And here comes the
biggest fake of all!"

01:32:54.986 --> 01:32:57.781
So, I'm gonna be launched
in this thing, huh?

01:32:57.864 --> 01:33:00.700
You can sound a
little happier about it.

01:33:00.825 --> 01:33:02.786
Yo, Shiro!

01:33:02.952 --> 01:33:07.457
One totally safe third stage.
A real bargain if you want it!

01:33:11.961 --> 01:33:15.173
Slowly... Slowly...
Okay, hold it!

01:33:16.216 --> 01:33:18.176
Like that! Like that!
Got it!

01:33:22.555 --> 01:33:24.015
Good morning, sir.

01:33:36.653 --> 01:33:41.574
Hello-everyone-this-is-astronaut-
Shirotsugh-Lhadatt. I-am...

01:33:41.658 --> 01:33:43.785
Say it properly!

01:33:43.910 --> 01:33:46.996
Oh, like anyone actually
listens to microwave broadcasts!

01:34:00.885 --> 01:34:03.263
Okay, push!

01:34:11.437 --> 01:34:13.106
It's finished!

01:34:18.361 --> 01:34:22.282
This is astronaut
Shirotsugh Lhadatt.

01:34:22.365 --> 01:34:27.203
I am currently in orbit,
flying 200 ren above our world...

01:34:28.246 --> 01:34:30.039
Can't sleep, huh?

01:34:30.748 --> 01:34:34.586
About this time tomorrow, you'll
have flown straight into history.

01:34:36.254 --> 01:34:38.715
The guys who were helping with
the construction today.

01:34:38.840 --> 01:34:41.384
They found tons of sea shells.

01:34:41.467 --> 01:34:44.179
Oh? Why are they here?

01:34:44.262 --> 01:34:46.389
Why do you think they are?

01:34:47.015 --> 01:34:50.894
A long time ago, a stone age tribe
used to dump their garbage here.

01:34:51.019 --> 01:34:54.355
Funny, isn't it?
This modern rocket of ours...

01:34:54.439 --> 01:34:57.192
is standing in a
prehistoric trash heap!

01:34:57.859 --> 01:35:00.987
Well, I'll bet those stone
age guys never thought...

01:35:01.070 --> 01:35:04.032
their garbage dump would
be used to launch a spaceship.

01:35:05.074 --> 01:35:10.705
What do you think they'll be
finding here in 10,000 years?

01:35:11.915 --> 01:35:15.376
A truly historic pile of
steel frames and concrete...

01:35:15.460 --> 01:35:18.504
mixed in with
somebody else's leftovers.

01:35:21.883 --> 01:35:24.093
Yeah, this Majaho over
at Guria Observatory.

01:35:24.219 --> 01:35:26.179
Get me the General!

01:35:26.763 --> 01:35:27.096
- What is it?

01:35:27.096 --> 01:35:28.973
- What is it?
- How are things going?

01:35:29.432 --> 01:35:31.684
We're crawling with Central
Intelligence guys on this end.

01:35:31.768 --> 01:35:34.979
They keep asking if we've changed
the launch time every one maal.

01:35:35.104 --> 01:35:40.026
Right, I understand!
All right... Don't worry.

01:35:41.027 --> 01:35:42.320
Just hang UP!

01:36:05.218 --> 01:36:07.220
The red one?
No, the yellow?

01:36:07.303 --> 01:36:08.471
That one.

01:36:09.430 --> 01:36:11.349
<i>Good morning,
ladies and gentlemen.</i>

01:36:11.474 --> 01:36:14.435
<i>Launch day is finally here.</i>

01:36:14.519 --> 01:36:16.062
Good morning, sir!

01:36:19.565 --> 01:36:21.150
Where's the
launch commander?

01:36:21.276 --> 01:36:22.610
- In the control bunker...

01:36:22.610 --> 01:36:24.070
- In the control bunker...
- The schedule controller?

01:36:24.153 --> 01:36:24.988
- Sleeping, sir.

01:36:24.988 --> 01:36:26.239
- Sleeping, sir.
- Then wake him!

01:36:26.322 --> 01:36:28.157
We've been working round
the clock for 4 days, sir.

01:36:28.241 --> 01:36:29.450
Everyone's exhausted!

01:36:30.034 --> 01:36:31.953
I'm moving the
launch time up two <i>maal.</i>

01:36:32.453 --> 01:36:36.207
Impossible! We need at least half
a day to complete preparations!

01:36:36.666 --> 01:36:39.085
There are signs that Central Intelligence...

01:36:39.168 --> 01:36:41.713
has been leaking
the information.

01:36:41.838 --> 01:36:43.506
I'm afraid we might
be attacked tonight.

01:36:43.631 --> 01:36:47.218
But, how? We can't take out
anything from the schedule!

01:36:48.011 --> 01:36:49.846
We'll shorten the
engineering check.

01:36:49.929 --> 01:36:52.223
Cut 124 pages from
the beginning of the sixth book.

01:36:52.682 --> 01:36:55.184
Do not tell the observatory
until the last possible moment.

01:36:55.310 --> 01:36:57.145
Have Shirotsugh take a shower.

01:36:57.228 --> 01:37:00.815
Just a minute, sir!
That's going too far.

01:37:00.898 --> 01:37:04.402
It's dangerous!
General! I'm against this!

01:37:04.527 --> 01:37:07.196
It's okay. I'll go.

01:37:07.655 --> 01:37:09.699
It'll be a lot more dangerous
if the enemy shows up here.

01:37:09.824 --> 01:37:12.702
No one's gonna stop them
anyways, right?

01:37:19.709 --> 01:37:25.882
This operation's objective is the
capture of the launch facilities.

01:37:25.965 --> 01:37:31.387
Do not lose sight of this in the raid.

01:37:31.471 --> 01:37:37.643
You will be refueling once,
from the air fortress, over Rimada.

01:37:37.727 --> 01:37:39.729
Empty your pockets on this one!

01:37:39.979 --> 01:37:41.981
Luck be with us!

01:37:43.441 --> 01:37:45.193
Hurry up with the fuel!

01:37:45.276 --> 01:37:47.987
Check on the third stage
and its connections!

01:37:50.365 --> 01:37:53.534
Scratch that! We won't
know unless we put fuel into it.

01:38:15.598 --> 01:38:17.225
Hey. Let's go.

01:38:18.935 --> 01:38:22.230
Begin liquid oxygen onload.

01:38:28.277 --> 01:38:33.032
<i>Would all stations please
report in and confirm status?</i>

01:39:03.354 --> 01:39:04.772
<i>Message in from Rimada.</i>

01:39:04.856 --> 01:39:07.358
<i>"Formation has made
contact with air fortress."</i>

01:39:15.825 --> 01:39:18.995
I know. We'll run into them
in the sky above the site.

01:39:19.120 --> 01:39:21.789
Gotcha... Roger. Moving out.

01:39:28.504 --> 01:39:31.174
Domurhot, phone call from
the launch site for you.

01:39:32.925 --> 01:39:34.177
We're launching early.

01:39:34.427 --> 01:39:36.179
Start getting the satellite
tracking systems ready.

01:39:36.471 --> 01:39:38.181
We're gonna outsmart them!

01:39:43.394 --> 01:39:45.188
How much more'?

01:39:46.189 --> 01:39:48.483
I'm finishing up now.
Yeah, that's got it.

01:40:04.165 --> 01:40:06.459
Good, we're on schedule.

01:40:09.587 --> 01:40:12.215
<i>Launch personnel report
to control bunker.</i>

01:40:12.340 --> 01:40:15.927
<i>All other personnel, move
to your regular positions.</i>

01:40:18.554 --> 01:40:19.764
<i>Check completed.</i>

01:40:19.889 --> 01:40:22.308
Activating
pressurization pumps.

01:40:31.025 --> 01:40:31.901
Activated.

01:40:31.984 --> 01:40:33.653
Tank #1 cabin
pressure, normal.

01:40:33.736 --> 01:40:35.279
Fuel, normal.

01:40:35.947 --> 01:40:37.657
Voltage, normal.

01:40:37.740 --> 01:40:39.242
Oil pressure, normal.

01:40:39.408 --> 01:40:41.744
Main support inclination standard to spec.

01:40:45.665 --> 01:40:48.084
Did we get the weather
report from the airship yet?

01:40:52.129 --> 01:40:54.257
Warrant Officer Tenz Kovikh.

01:40:54.382 --> 01:40:56.634
Frontier Guard,
Tayan Observation Squad.

01:40:56.759 --> 01:40:59.011
Please pass along withdrawal
orders to all personnel.

01:40:59.095 --> 01:41:01.138
We're evacuating this area.

01:41:01.389 --> 01:41:03.849
What are you talking about?
We're about to launch now.

01:41:03.933 --> 01:41:05.309
It's too late.

01:41:05.434 --> 01:41:07.436
I'm sorry, sir.

01:41:08.271 --> 01:41:10.106
This place is about to
become a battlefield.

01:41:10.189 --> 01:41:12.400
The occupation forces
have crossed the river.

01:41:12.483 --> 01:41:13.776
What'?!

01:41:14.110 --> 01:41:16.779
Our border patrols
are under attack.

01:41:34.130 --> 01:41:35.673
Damn it all!

01:41:40.511 --> 01:41:43.097
What was that?
I couldn't hear you.

01:41:43.180 --> 01:41:46.434
<i>The launch is scrubbed. They're
attacking sooner than we thought.</i>

01:41:46.517 --> 01:41:49.979
What are you talking about?
We're just going to run away?

01:41:50.104 --> 01:41:53.524
They want this thing!
They're not gonna shoot at it!

01:41:53.649 --> 01:41:55.860
They might if
we try to launch!

01:41:55.985 --> 01:41:58.112
Enough! We're pulling
you out of there.

01:42:05.620 --> 01:42:10.374
We have to do this.
I hate it as much as you do.

01:42:12.084 --> 01:42:15.254
And I really thought we
could do it this time.

01:42:15.379 --> 01:42:17.465
We may as well
get out while we can.

01:42:17.548 --> 01:42:22.303
This foolish thing... It's not
worth risking your lives for.

01:42:23.262 --> 01:42:24.722
Just give it up!

01:42:25.348 --> 01:42:27.224
<i>Wait a minute here.
I don't believe this!</i>

01:42:27.350 --> 01:42:29.518
<i>What do you mean,
"foolish "?</i>

01:42:29.602 --> 01:42:32.688
<i>If we stop here, then what
are we? Even bigger fools!</i>

01:42:32.772 --> 01:42:36.442
<i>You're just going
to throw it all away?</i>

01:42:36.525 --> 01:42:38.778
<i>Everything we've been
able to accomplish?</i>

01:42:38.861 --> 01:42:41.030
<i>Don't say everything
we've done here is stupid.</i>

01:42:41.155 --> 01:42:42.114
<i>It's wonderful!</i>

01:42:42.365 --> 01:42:44.867
<i>Wonderful enough to get
us into the history books!</i>

01:42:44.992 --> 01:42:46.077
<i>I'll still do it.</i>

01:42:46.202 --> 01:42:48.871
<i>Even if I die, I want to
at least try to launch!</i>

01:42:48.996 --> 01:42:50.706
<i>Anyone who wants out can go!</i>

01:42:50.790 --> 01:42:52.124
<i>I will do this!</i>

01:42:52.708 --> 01:42:55.169
<i>I am god damned
ready to do this!!</i>

01:42:56.504 --> 01:42:59.131
<i>All sections, talk to me!</i>

01:42:59.674 --> 01:43:01.092
Voltage, check.

01:43:02.051 --> 01:43:03.094
Oil pressure, check.

01:43:03.761 --> 01:43:05.096
Pumps, standing by.

01:43:06.097 --> 01:43:07.098
Fuel, check!

01:43:09.725 --> 01:43:12.603
Platform is conditionally
"go" for launch.

01:43:19.777 --> 01:43:21.612
Let's give it a try.

01:43:22.071 --> 01:43:23.114
Return to countdown!

01:43:23.489 --> 01:43:25.491
All right!!

01:44:07.366 --> 01:44:08.784
Mount 'em up!

01:44:10.786 --> 01:44:13.622
I guess the crew will
share their ship's fate.

01:44:13.706 --> 01:44:15.207
Move out!

01:44:21.380 --> 01:44:22.089
<i>Dispatch from Magitsu.</i>

01:44:22.173 --> 01:44:24.925
<i>We are now 02 from target.</i>

01:44:29.430 --> 01:44:33.058
<i>Look sharp people!
Enemy fighters right above us!</i>

01:44:46.906 --> 01:44:49.784
Pump restart is good.
No problems.

01:44:50.618 --> 01:44:52.787
We're in primary
launch stages.

01:44:56.582 --> 01:44:58.250
<i>Engineer Corps ETA:</i>

01:44:58.334 --> 01:45:00.085
<i>Delay of 52.</i>

01:45:13.557 --> 01:45:15.976
Stabilizing gyro.
Give me a reading.

01:45:16.936 --> 01:45:18.854
Inertial Navigation System
reads as follows...

01:45:18.938 --> 01:45:24.652
North, 2.8 degrees, 36 minutes, 30.32 seconds.

01:45:36.038 --> 01:45:38.207
Cabin pressure rising, normal!

01:45:53.389 --> 01:45:55.057
402 to go!

01:45:55.182 --> 01:45:57.810
I can see smoke
from the shooting.

01:46:13.534 --> 01:46:16.078
Spaceship systems are
now running autonomous.

01:46:16.203 --> 01:46:19.415
373 to go!

01:46:42.771 --> 01:46:44.565
Closing main oxygen
escape valve.

01:46:44.648 --> 01:46:46.442
102 to go.

01:46:46.567 --> 01:46:49.153
<i>Confirm power supplies
are charged and ready.</i>

01:46:53.949 --> 01:46:55.910
Starting water flow
to launch platform!

01:47:01.123 --> 01:47:04.209
80 to go.
We're in final stages.

01:47:04.293 --> 01:47:06.879
Everyone take
your positions!

01:47:10.591 --> 01:47:11.759
<i>' TO </i>

01:47:11.759 --> 01:47:13.010
- 60 to go!
- Let's see...!

01:47:16.388 --> 01:47:17.848
Engine ignition in 20...

01:47:19.016 --> 01:47:20.142
19...

01:47:20.267 --> 01:47:21.393
18...

01:47:21.477 --> 01:47:22.811
<i>17...</i>

01:47:22.895 --> 01:47:23.938
16...

01:47:24.021 --> 01:47:25.272
<i>15...</i>

01:47:25.356 --> 01:47:26.482
14...

01:47:26.607 --> 01:47:27.816
13...

01:47:27.900 --> 01:47:29.068
12...

01:47:29.151 --> 01:47:30.361
11...

01:47:30.486 --> 01:47:31.779
10...

01:47:31.862 --> 01:47:33.155
9...

01:47:33.280 --> 01:47:34.490
8...

01:47:34.573 --> 01:47:35.824
<i>7...</i>

01:47:35.950 --> 01:47:37.076
6...

01:47:37.159 --> 01:47:38.410
<i>5...</i>

01:47:38.494 --> 01:47:39.745
4...

01:47:39.828 --> 01:47:40.996
3...

01:47:41.121 --> 01:47:42.289
<i>'2...</i>

01:47:42.373 --> 01:47:43.540
1 -

01:47:49.296 --> 01:47:50.214
It's exploded!

01:47:50.339 --> 01:47:52.883
So far, so good.
Let's do it!

01:49:04.204 --> 01:49:11.003
4000, 4500, 5000,
5500, 6000...

01:49:18.844 --> 01:49:21.180
First stage has
successfully detached.

01:49:43.410 --> 01:49:45.204
Third stage ignition has begun.

01:49:45.287 --> 01:49:52.377
12000, 12500, 13000, 13500...
Ignition complete!

01:49:58.592 --> 01:50:00.719
<i>This is Guria Observatory.</i>

01:50:01.178 --> 01:50:03.722
It's confirmed.
It's achieved orbital velocity.

01:50:03.806 --> 01:50:05.641
He's in orbit!

01:50:05.808 --> 01:50:07.976
<i>WE'VE DONE IT!!!</i>

01:50:54.523 --> 01:50:58.026
City lights...
I wonder where they are...?

01:51:06.577 --> 01:51:08.537
They really do
look like stars...

01:51:16.044 --> 01:51:20.048
ls anybody down there
listening to this broadcast?

01:51:20.215 --> 01:51:25.179
This is mankind's first astronaut.

01:51:26.054 --> 01:51:28.932
The human race
has just taken...

01:51:29.057 --> 01:51:31.727
its first step into
the world of the stars.

01:51:32.227 --> 01:51:35.022
Like the oceans and
the mountains before...

01:51:35.105 --> 01:51:38.108
space too was once
just God's domain.

01:51:38.233 --> 01:51:41.361
As it becomes a familiar place
for us, it'll probably end up...

01:51:41.445 --> 01:51:44.239
as bad as everywhere
else we've meddled.

01:51:44.698 --> 01:51:47.743
We've spoiled the land,
we've fouled the air.

01:51:47.826 --> 01:51:51.079
Yet we still seek
new places to live...

01:51:51.163 --> 01:51:53.498
and so now we
journey out to space.

01:51:53.916 --> 01:51:59.254
How far will we be allowed
to push our limit?

01:52:00.547 --> 01:52:05.802
Please...
Whoever's listening to me...

01:52:06.094 --> 01:52:08.931
How you do it doesn't
matter, just please...

01:52:09.306 --> 01:52:15.103
Give some thanks for
mankind's arrival here.

01:52:16.688 --> 01:52:20.776
Please, show us mercy
and forgive us.

01:52:22.110 --> 01:52:26.657
Don't let the way ahead
be one of darkness.

01:52:27.282 --> 01:52:30.494
As we stumble down the path of our sinful history...

01:52:31.286 --> 01:52:36.583
let there always be one
shining star to show the way.

01:56:02.122 --> 01:56:05.167
Please, listen
to God's teachings.
